Nodeloris is a dual-use network security research and connection-testing utility for Node.js.

The package creates TCP or TLS connections to a user-specified host and can maintain multiple concurrent connections for controlled testing of network services.

This functionality is intended for authorized security research, defensive testing, development, benchmarking, and testing of systems owned or explicitly authorized by the user.

Users are responsible for obtaining authorization before testing systems they do not own or operate.

Nodeloris does not contain malware, persistence mechanisms, credential theft functionality, spyware, or mechanisms intended to compromise or maintain unauthorized access to systems.
